1904"] ". He would win again in " [:a {:href "/results/56488"} "1908"] " in this event, and also the " [:a {:href "/results/56862"} "1912 Olympic variant with both hands"] ". He would also win the AAU championship in 1907-1910."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The rules in force were those of the United States, rather than Britain.  The jury had a difficult time deciding who was putting the shot and who was throwing it, the primary offender apparently being the Finn " [:a {:href "/athletes/67619"} "Verner Järvinen"] ", who was favored in Rose/Horgan’s absence, but had no fair efforts.  In the absence of the world’s top putters, " [:a {:href "/athletes/79031"} "Martin Sheridan"] " won the event, but his mark was mediocre.  Either Rose or Horgan would have surpassed it easily."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Distance"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "615"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/79031"} "Martin Sheridan"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "12.325"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "787"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/79701"} "Mihály Dávid"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/HUN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/HUN.png"}] "HUN"]] [:td {} "11.830"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "381"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/76253"} "Eric Lemming"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SWE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws